# MotionLab Environment Configuration Example
# MotionLab is an offline-first, client-side motion graphics application.
# Local editing, Canvas rendering, and timeline keyframing run 100% locally in the browser.
#
# ==============================================================================
# Google Gemini AI Integration (Prompt-to-Motion Generator)
# ==============================================================================
# To enable the AI Prompt-to-Motion Generator, obtain a free or paid API key
# from Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/) and configure it below.
#
# NOTE: Kept strictly server-side! Never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for API keys.
# MULTI-KEY SUPPORT:
# Anda dapat memasukkan satu key atau banyak key dipisahkan koma (comma-separated).
# Sistem akan otomatis melakukan round-robin load balancing dan auto-failover jika terjadi limit kuota (429/ResourceExhausted).
# Format: GEMINI_API_KEY=key1,key2,key3,key4
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# ==============================================================================
# Local Build / Android Userspace Settings (Optional)
# ==============================================================================
# On native Android Termux/userspace environments, the SWC WASM binding path is set locally:
# NEXT_TEST_WASM_DIR="./node_modules/@next/swc-wasm-nodejs"
#
# When deployed on Vercel or standard Linux/macOS/Windows x64 servers, Next.js automatically
# uses native binary bindings without needing any environment variable.
